<title>ITALY: Bell exercises rights in Omnitel stake deal.</title>
<headline>Bell exercises rights in Omnitel stake deal.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. telecommunications group Bell Atlantic has exercised its pre-emptive rights to buy an 8.26 percent stake in Omnitel Sistemi Radiocellulari (OSR) that German group Mannesmann had previous agreed to buy.</p>
<p>Bell Atlantic, which already has a 16.7 percent stake in OSR, said it was exercising its rights to buy the stake provided other OSR shareholders did not exercise their rights, a statement from information and technology group Olivetti said.</p>
<p>Olivetti is the major shareholder in OSR, which in turn holds a 70 percent stake in Omnitel, Italy's second mobile telephone company.</p>
</text>
